WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
If you're new to AI, or you've
tried it a few times and

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.930
want to get more from it,
this is a good place to begin.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.050
These are the tips we wish
we'd had when we started.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.670
They're small habits
that can save time,

5
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.550
make AI easier to work with and help
you remember what you've learnt.

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.270
Tip one is about using your voice,

7
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.190
both to talk to AI and to hear
its answers when that suits you.

8
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.580
It can make using
AI feel more natural

9
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.740
and give your eyes a
break from the screen.

10
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.570
Tip two is to treat AI like a
colleague who's just joined your team.

11
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.620
Giving it a clear sense
of what you need helps

12
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.770
it produce something
that's useful to you.

13
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.240
Tip three is to ask AI to
help write your prompt,

14
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.780
the request you give it.

15
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.680
It can help you find the words for a

16
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.790
task when you're
unsure where to begin.

17
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.180
Tip four is to give AI
something to work from.

18
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.340
An example makes the style, length
or layout you're after clearer,

19
00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.010
so there's less room for it to
misunderstand what you have in mind.

20
00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.190
Tip five is to keep a record
of what you're learning.

21
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.710
A notebook gives you somewhere
to return to useful prompts,

22
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.520
discoveries and ideas,
so you don't have

23
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.810
to remember everything
or start again.

24
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.210
Tip six is to begin with manageable
tasks and keep costs low.

25
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.160
That gives you space to
build confidence and find

26
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.320
out what's useful before
spending more time or money.

27
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.840
Tip seven is to look at our labs
before choosing which AI to use.

28
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.440
The labs compare
different versions of AI,

29
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.550
called models, on the
same everyday tasks.

30
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.180
You can see their
answers side by side.

31
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:35.730
That helps you choose one that
suits your work and save money.

32
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.520
After those seven tips,

33
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.080
you'll find ten shorter
habits worth picking up,

34
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.270
followed by the vital tips from
the first month of the course.

35
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.820
They're there to help you
avoid common frustrations

36
00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.130
and get more from your
practice as you go.

37
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.930
Scroll down and take
your time with the tips.

38
00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.470
Put one into practice.

39
00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.110
Try our labs too.

40
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.600
And if you'd like to keep learning
with us, sign up to the course.

41
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.410
You can cancel any time.
